  "summary": "Reconciled all 5 St. Brigid discharges per RBC-TOC-02. Each has a progress note.\n\nWalter Kim (pt-0005, note doc-t0016):\n- Furosemide changed to 40 mg BID (mr-t0001). This follows the signed addendum doc-00009.\n- KCl stopped (mr-00076).\n- Pantoprazole not ordered because it was a formulary substitution; home omeprazole kept.\n- Lisinopril (mr-00072): kept on hold at first because K was 5.4 on 10/21. Resumed after the repeat BMP arrived 10/23 with K 4.7 and SCr 1.21.\n- An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg BID was not acted on.\n- Task-t0006 is now moot (Task tools can't close it); I messaged you that it can be closed (comm-t0021).\n\nTerence Stark (pt-0004, note doc-t0017):\n- Carvedilol first changed to 12.5 mg BID per the summary. A signed addendum then arrived reversing it (bradycardia), so the order is back to 6.25 mg BID (mr-t0011).\n- Flagged to you: atorvastatin 80 mg was only ~24% filled, so no change (comm-t0008).\n- Flagged to you: glipizide from an outside endocrinologist isn't addressed in the discharge papers and has no clinic order (comm-t0009).\n\nEarnest Roberts (pt-0044, note doc-t0018):\n- Lisinopril resumed once SCr was 1.08, then put back on hold when K 5.5 arrived 10/23.\n- Task for you due 10/27 (task-t0014).\n\nGerald Whitcomb (pt-0069, note doc-t0019):\n- Lisinopril resumed once SCr was 1.12, then put back on hold when the 10/22 K of 5.4 arrived.\n- Task for you due 10/26 (task-t0015).\n\nLorraine Pruitt (pt-0067, note doc-t0020):\n- Metformin stays on hold. The only SCr is from the hospital stay, and the discharge condition needs a post-discharge result.\n- Task for you due 10/24, when the BMP is expected (task-t0007).\n\nUnchanged meds were continued as documented. I closed the 5 arrival inbox items. Nothing else new came in.",
